### Real-World Implementation: Provider Directory Search Caching

**Business Context**: State Medicaid portals provide provider directory search allowing members to find doctors, hospitals, and pharmacies accepting Medicaid. Provider data changes infrequently (monthly updates) but is queried millions of times daily. Without caching, provider directory searches averaged 2.8 seconds response time, causing 18% search abandonment.

**Implementation Approach**:

```csharp
public class ProviderSearchService
{
    private readonly ICacheService _cache;
    private readonly IProviderRepository _repository;

    public async Task<ProviderSearchResults> SearchProvidersAsync(
        string tenantId, ProviderSearchRequest request)
    {
        // Generate cache key from search parameters
        var cacheKey = GenerateSearchCacheKey(tenantId, request);

        // Check cache first
        var cachedResults = await _cache.GetAsync<ProviderSearchResults>(cacheKey);
        if (cachedResults != null)
        {
            return cachedResults;
        }

        // Cache miss - execute search against database
        var results = await _repository.SearchAsync(tenantId, request);

        // Cache results for 1 hour (providers change infrequently)
        await _cache.SetAsync(
            cacheKey,
            results,
            TimeSpan.FromHours(1));

        return results;
    }

    private string GenerateSearchCacheKey(string tenantId, ProviderSearchRequest request)
    {
        // Include all search parameters in cache key for uniqueness
        return $"{tenantId}:provider:search:" +
               $"{request.Specialty}:{request.ZipCode}:{request.Radius}:" +
               $"{request.AcceptingNewPatients}:{request.Page}";
    }
}
```

**Results Achieved** (California Medicaid portal, January-March 2024):
- **Response Time**: Reduced from 2,800ms (P95) to 320ms (P95) - 89% improvement
- **Cache Hit Rate**: 87% of searches served from cache
- **Database Load**: Reduced from 1.2M daily queries to 156K - 87% reduction
- **Search Abandonment**: Decreased from 18% to 6% - 67% improvement
- **Infrastructure Costs**: Saved $8,200/month by reducing database tier from P6 to P2

**Before/After Comparison**:

| Metric | Before Caching | After Caching | Improvement |
|--------|---------------|---------------|-------------|
| P95 Response Time | 2,800ms | 320ms | 89% faster |
| P50 Response Time | 1,850ms | 85ms | 95% faster |
| Daily Database Queries | 1,200,000 | 156,000 | 87% reduction |
| Search Abandonment Rate | 18% | 6% | 67% improvement |
| Monthly Infrastructure Cost | $14,500 | $6,300 | 57% reduction |
| Cache Hit Rate | N/A | 87% | N/A |

